# =====================================================================
#  xmssidx_resume.la — proves the register survives PROCESS DEATH.
#
#  This is the check `xmssidx.la`'s own MAIN structurally cannot make: it
#  initialises its state file, so everything it verifies happens inside one
#  process. Durability is a claim about what survives when the process does
#  not, and only a SECOND process can witness it.
#
#  So this module deliberately does NOT initialise. It reads whatever the
#  previous process left and reserves once. Run straight after xmssidx.la
#  (which leaves the file at 3) it must hand out exactly 3 — not 0.
#
#  ★ A register that kept its counter in memory, or that re-created its state
#  file on read, would pass every check in xmssidx.la and fail here by handing
#  out 0 — and handing out 0 a second time is the reuse that breaks the key.
#  If the state file is ABSENT this halts loudly via read_file, which is the
#  correct behaviour and is asserted separately by the gate.
# =====================================================================
import("xmssidx.la")
glyph P = "xmssidx_test.state"
glyph H = 2
glyph MAIN = print(concat(concat("xmssidx resume: reserved=")(int_to_str(IDX_RESERVE(P)(H))))
                         (concat(" next=")(int_to_str(IDX_READ(P)))))
